xnu 0357: print the file behind each allocation and each free

0356 named the process that frees blocks the bitmap does not own, and on a root
written from the fsck-verified image 152 such frees came from fifteen daemons,
almost all of them a single block -- so the accounting is the lead, not a
service. A process name still does not say which file lost its bits.

This prints the catalog file id, the first 43 bytes of the name and the fork on
both sides, for the first 24 operands of each: an extension as BlockAllocate()
hands it out, and a truncate as BlockDeallocate() takes it back. A free whose
file was never announced with that range, in the same boot, points at the step
that dropped the bit; with both lines the diagnosis is a diff, not a theory.

diff --git a/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/FileExtentMapping.c b/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/FileExtentMapping.c
--- a/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/FileExtentMapping.c
+++ b/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/FileExtentMapping.c
@@ -1078,6 +1078,31 @@
